  "summary": "Lucas County commissioners voted to rescind a previously-approved $250,000, four-year Flock ALPR contract with the sheriff's office after Commissioner Pete Gerken reconsidered, citing mass surveillance concerns and chilling effects on minority communities. Commissioners Gerken and Lopez voted to rescind; Sobecki preferred to wait for more information.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "It is inappropriate for the sheriff, in the time of budget constraints on all of us, to spend $250,000 to mass surveil our community without any intended outcome",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Having time to reflect on my vote, I would like to rescind the approval of that agreement",
